== Attacks and abilities ==
{{For|strategies for defeating Dvergr|Aggressive creature strategies#Dvergr}}Due to range requirements, many attacks from every variant of mages are possible to disable by standing directly against the caster. Both the fire mages and the ice mage share a melee attack.

==== Melee ====
Pokes the player with the hilt of their staff (70 [[Damage types#Blunt|Blunt]] damage). This is accessible every 4 seconds when within 0.5-2.5 meters of a player. Despite being a straight thrust, this attack hits a horizontal arc 2.5 meters long and 90 degrees across.

===Fire mages===
Fire mages wear a red robe lined with gold and carry a pronged, fiery-red staff. They have two unique attacks:

==== Fireball ====
Brings their staff around and then sweeps down to launch a single fireball that inflicts the [[Burning]] status (130 [[Damage types#Fire|Fire]] damage). The fireball travels at 15 meters per second for up to 10 seconds before despawning. It is generated with a spread of 1–10 degrees. This attack can be used every 6 seconds when within a 1–15 meters of a player. If it hits the ground instead of a player, it creates a 6-meter radius circular blast that expands outward (100 [[Damage types#Fire|Fire]] damage).

==== Clusterbomb ====
Waves their staff for a few seconds before raising it up higher to launch a shower of nine fireballs in various directions that inflict the [[Burning]] status (100 [[Damage types#Fire|Fire]] damage each). Each fireball travels at 11 meters per second for up to 10 seconds before despawning. They originate from a point 2.5 meters off the ground and have a spread of 40–50 degrees. This attack can be used every 35 seconds when within 5–30 meters of a player. On impact with the ground, these fireballs create 3-meter radius circular fields of fire (100 [[Damage types#Fire|Fire]] damage).

===Ice mages===
Ice mages wear a blue robe lined with silver and carry a staff tipped with a glowing blue ice shard. They have two unique attacks:

==== Icebolt ====
Stabs forward with their staff to launch three balls of ice at the player which inflict the [[Frost]] status (200 [[Damage types#Frost|Frost]] damage). Each ball of ice travels at 15 meters per second for up to 4 seconds before despawning and has a spread of 8–15 degrees. This attack can be used every 6 seconds when within 1–15 meters of a player.

==== Nova ====
Slams their staff down to create an outward expanding circle with a radius of 5 meters, which inflicts the [[Frost]] status (150 [[Damage types#Frost|Frost]] damage). This attack can be used every 7 seconds when within 0–7 meters of a player.

===Support mages===
Support mages wear a yellow-and-brown robe lined with gold and carry a staff tipped with a [[Dvergr Lantern]]. They have three unique abilities:

==== Buff ====
Lifts their staff up before slamming it into the ground to apply the [[Dvergr power]] status to themselves and allies within 8 meters for 20 seconds (+20% to all [[Skills]]). This ability can be used every 45 seconds when within 1–15 meters of an ally. 

==== Heal ====
Draws a half-circle on the ground before lifting their staff in the air to apply the [[Dvergr heal]] status to themselves and allies within 4.32 meters for 4 seconds (400 health ticking every 0.5 seconds). This ability can be used every 10 seconds when within 1–15 meters of an ally. 

==== Mistile ====
Smashes the ground with their staff to create 1–3 [[Mistile|Mistiles]] within a 3-meter radius around the caster; a max of nine can be active at once. These orbs have 1 health and track the player to deal damage on impact (150 [[Damage types#Blunt|Blunt]] damage). These can be summoned every 35 seconds when within 1–15 meters from a player. The Mistiles themselves deal damage in a 1.5 meter sphere when within 1 meter of the player.

